WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.013
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:08.642
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:16.436
Unit four: Emotions & Expressing Feelings. In this unit, you will describe your feelings and say when you feel them.

4
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.114
Feel.

5
00:00:18.814 --> 00:00:20.442
Feel means to have an emotion.

6
00:00:20.742 --> 00:00:22.893
I feel happy when I see my friends.

7
00:00:23.593 --> 00:00:25.804
Your turn. Say: Feel.

8
00:00:28.504 --> 00:00:29.122
Feel.

9
00:00:30.117 --> 00:00:31.083
Nervous.

10
00:00:31.783 --> 00:00:34.015
Nervous means a little afraid or worried.

11
00:00:34.315 --> 00:00:36.395
I feel nervous before a test.

12
00:00:37.095 --> 00:00:39.446
Your turn. Say: Nervous.

13
00:00:42.146 --> 00:00:43.066
Nervous.

14
00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:44.877
Confident.

15
00:00:45.577 --> 00:00:48.064
Confident means sure that you can do something well.

16
00:00:48.364 --> 00:00:50.410
I feel confident when I practise.

17
00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:53.902
Your turn. Say: Confident.

18
00:00:56.602 --> 00:00:57.556
Confident.

19
00:00:58.550 --> 00:00:59.203
Calm.

20
00:00:59.903 --> 00:01:02.216
Calm means quiet and relaxed, not worried.

21
00:01:02.516 --> 00:01:04.388
Take a deep breath and stay calm.

22
00:01:05.088 --> 00:01:07.821
Your turn. Say: Calm.

23
00:01:10.521 --> 00:01:11.139
Calm.

24
00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.093
Frustrated.

25
00:01:13.793 --> 00:01:16.710
Frustrated means upset because something is not working.

26
00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.659
I feel frustrated when my computer is slow.

27
00:01:20.359 --> 00:01:23.499
Your turn. Say: Frustrated.

28
00:01:26.199 --> 00:01:27.201
Frustrated.

29
00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:29.276
Relieved.

30
00:01:29.976 --> 00:01:32.498
Relieved means happy because a worry has ended.

31
00:01:32.798 --> 00:01:34.751
I felt relieved after the exam.

32
00:01:35.451 --> 00:01:38.452
Your turn. Say: Relieved.

33
00:01:41.152 --> 00:01:42.187
Relieved.

34
00:01:43.183 --> 00:01:44.289
Express.

35
00:01:44.989 --> 00:01:47.697
Express means to show or say what you think or feel.

36
00:01:47.997 --> 00:01:49.996
It's good to express your feelings.

37
00:01:50.696 --> 00:01:53.244
Your turn. Say: Express.

38
00:01:55.944 --> 00:01:57.131
Express.

39
00:01:58.117 --> 00:01:59.129
Understand.

40
00:01:59.829 --> 00:02:02.572
Understand means to know why someone feels something.

41
00:02:02.872 --> 00:02:04.825
My mum understands how I feel.

42
00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:08.653
Your turn. Say: Understand.

43
00:02:11.353 --> 00:02:12.494
Understand.

44
00:02:13.483 --> 00:02:15.576
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:15.876 --> 00:02:18.525
Sreypich, how do you feel today?

46
00:02:19.817 --> 00:02:22.887
I feel a little nervous. I have a speaking test.

47
00:02:24.183 --> 00:02:25.765
When do you feel confident?

48
00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:29.468
I feel confident when I practise a lot.

49
00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.899
And how will you feel after the test?

50
00:02:34.183 --> 00:02:36.264
I'll feel relieved and very calm!

51
00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:40.815
Grammar focus: I feel plus adjective plus when.

52
00:02:41.115 --> 00:02:43.022
I feel nervous when I have a test.

53
00:02:43.322 --> 00:02:46.296
Use 'when' to explain the situation that gives you the feeling.

54
00:02:47.283 --> 00:02:50.354
Now read and listen. Talking About Feelings.

55
00:02:50.654 --> 00:02:52.909
Everyone has different feelings every day.

56
00:02:54.217 --> 00:02:56.901
I feel nervous when I speak in front of the class.

57
00:02:58.217 --> 00:03:01.203
I feel frustrated when I can't solve a math problem.

58
00:03:02.517 --> 00:03:05.979
When I express my feelings to my mum, she understands me.

59
00:03:07.283 --> 00:03:09.167
Then I feel calm and relieved.

60
00:03:10.483 --> 00:03:12.962
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:13.262 --> 00:03:15.737
I feel calm blank I listen to music.

62
00:03:16.037 --> 00:03:18.553
A, when. B, who. C, what.

63
00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.911
The answer is A: when.

64
00:03:25.417 --> 00:03:27.486
A little afraid or worried is blank.

65
00:03:27.786 --> 00:03:30.987
A, nervous. B, confident. C, relieved.

66
00:03:34.983 --> 00:03:37.041
The answer is A: nervous.

67
00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.851
Happy because a worry has ended is blank.

68
00:03:41.151 --> 00:03:45.803
A, relieved. B, frustrated. C, nervous.

69
00:03:49.817 --> 00:03:51.445
The answer is A: relieved.

70
00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:56.183
Now it's your turn to speak. When do you feel confident?

71
00:04:01.483 --> 00:04:07.537
I feel confident when I practise English with my friends. I feel nervous when I have a test, but I stay calm.

72
00:04:07.837 --> 00:04:09.488
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:14.854
Great work today! You learned eight new words and i feel plus adjective plus when.

74
00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:19.525
Today's value is self-awareness. Know your strengths and keep growing.

75
00:04:19.825 --> 00:04:22.326
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

76
00:04:22.626 --> 00:04:25.197
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

